{title: Crown Him with Many Crowns}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C]Crown Him with [**]many [F]crowns[**], the [C]Lamb u[F]pon His [G]throne[**]
Hark [C]how the [Am]heav'nly [D]anthem [G]drowns[**] all [**]music [D]but its [G]own[**]
A[C]wake, my [**]soul, and [F]sing[**] of [D]Him who [**]died for [G]thee[**]
And [C]hail Him [F]as thy [G]matchless [C]King through [F]all e[G]terni[C]ty [**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]life[**], who [C]triumphed [F]o'er the [G]grave[**]
And [C]rose vic[Am]torious [D]in the [G]strife for [**]those He [D]came to [G]save[**]
His [C]glories [**]now we [F]sing[**], who [D]died and [**]rose on [G]high
Who [C]died e[F]ternal [G]life to [C]bring and [F]lives that [G]death may [C]die[**]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]peace[**] whose [C]power a [F]scepter [G]sways[**]
From [C]pole to [Am]pole, that [D]wars may [G]cease and [**]all be [D]prayer and [G]praise[**]
His [C]reign shall [**]know no [F]end[**] and [D]round His [**]pierced [G]feet[**]
Fair [C]flowers of [F]para[G]dise ex[C]tend their [F]fragrance [G]ever [C]sweet[**].
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C]Crown Him the [**]Lord of [F]love[**], be[C]hold His [F]hands and [G]side[**]
Those [C]wounds yet [Am]visi[D]ble [G]above in [**]beauty [D]glori[G]fied[**]
All [C]hail Re[**]deemer, [F]hail[**], for [D]Thou hast [**]died for [G]me[**]
Thy [C]praise and [F]glory [G]shall not [C]fail through[F]out e[G]terni[C]ty[**]
{end_of_verse}
